This method of writing Japanese syllables by using characters for their Chinese sounds ({{tlit|ja|ongana}}) was supplemented with indirect methods in the complex mixed script of the ''[[Man'yōshū]]'' ({{circa|759}}).{{sfn|Seeley|1991|pp=49–53}}{{sfn|Miyake|2003|pp=20, 24–27}}{{sfn|Frellesvig|2010|pp=17–20}}

===Syllables===
In {{tlit|ja|man'yōgana}}, each Old Japanese syllable was represented by a Chinese character. Although any of several characters could be used for a given syllable, a careful analysis reveals that 88 syllables were distinguished in early Old Japanese, typified by the ''Kojiki'' songs:{{sfn|Miyake|2003|pp=49–51}}{{sfn|Frellesvig|2010|pp=26–27}}

